{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_ec831bc7-dffb-49af-9dcb-2e60f977273","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"gh issue view 7","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_ec831bc7-dffb-49af-9dcb-2e60f977273","simpleCommands":["gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"7"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 7"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch issue #7 body","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"a4b49908-1fff-436c-8b85-7053cc35540a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"a09b1b3c-34aa-45b4-baad-9b84151ab3b9"},"result":{"success":{"command":"gh issue view 7","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"title:\tTracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#6\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nnumber:\t7\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nThe tracer bullet for the CLI. A `delegate` binary built alongside the existing MCP server, which keeps working.\n\n- `delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`, validates input, writes the job's status record, starts a detached supervisor (own session and process group, stdio redirected), prints the job id and exits.\n- The supervisor runs cursor-agent, writes a heartbeat while running, parses the final STATUS line (including NEEDS_CONTEXT), and writes the terminal record with the full result (status, text, usage, cost, session id, plus what resume needs: model, cwd, capability).\n- `delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]` blocks until every record is terminal or the timeout passes, then prints each record.\n- read-only maps to cursor ask mode; read-write to `--sandbox disabled`; both keep `--force`.\n\nDrive this ticket's implementation through the recording script, saving the runs as fixtures.\n\nWeak point tested: a detached supervisor with the status record as the only source of truth.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `run` returns a job id while the job is still running, and the job finishes after `run` has exited.\n- [ ] The status record shows RUNNING with an advancing heartbeat, then the terminal result.\n- [ ] `watch` prints all named records once terminal, and exits at its timeout otherwise.\n- [ ] An unknown model is rejected with the list of valid ids.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests drive the binary as a process against the fake cursor-agent.\n- [ ] The existing MCP server and its tests still pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1425,"interleavedOutput":"title:\tTracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#6\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nnumber:\t7\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nThe tracer bullet for the CLI. A `delegate` binary built alongside the existing MCP server, which keeps working.\n\n- `delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`, validates input, writes the job's status record, starts a detached supervisor (own session and process group, stdio redirected), prints the job id and exits.\n- The supervisor runs cursor-agent, writes a heartbeat while running, parses the final STATUS line (including NEEDS_CONTEXT), and writes the terminal record with the full result (status, text, usage, cost, session id, plus what resume needs: model, cwd, capability).\n- `delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]` blocks until every record is terminal or the timeout passes, then prints each record.\n- read-only maps to cursor ask mode; read-write to `--sandbox disabled`; both keep `--force`.\n\nDrive this ticket's implementation through the recording script, saving the runs as fixtures.\n\nWeak point tested: a detached supervisor with the status record as the only source of truth.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `run` returns a job id while the job is still running, and the job finishes after `run` has exited.\n- [ ] The status record shows RUNNING with an advancing heartbeat, then the terminal result.\n- [ ] `watch` prints all named records once terminal, and exits at its timeout otherwise.\n- [ ] An unknown model is rejected with the list of valid ids.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests drive the binary as a process against the fake cursor-agent.\n- [ ] The existing MCP server and its tests still pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1200},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch issue #7 body"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_ec831bc7-dffb-49af-9dcb-2e60f977273","startedAtMs":"1790844187359","completedAtMs":"1790844188937"},"model_call_id":"a09b1b3c-34aa-45b4-baad-9b84151ab3b9-1-04kg","session_id":"a4b49908-1fff-436c-8b85-7053cc35540a","timestamp_ms":1790844188879}
